        "mission_intent": "We need to develop a comprehensive Security Assessment Capability Specification for our vulnerability assessment team, aligned with NIST SP 800-115 guidance on target identification and analysis. The spec should define minimum baseline skill requirements for each of the following techniques: network discovery, network port and service identification, vulnerability scanning, and wireless scanning. For network discovery, assessors must demonstrate general TCP/IP and networking knowledge plus proficiency with both passive and active discovery tools. For port and service identification, require TCP/IP knowledge, familiarity with ports and protocols across multiple operating systems, ability to operate port scanning tools, and demonstrated capability to interpret tool output. For vulnerability scanning, require all of the above plus knowledge of known vulnerabilities across platforms and the ability to use and configure automated scanning tools. For wireless scanning, the spec must address detection of unauthorized devices, identification of wireless signals beyond organizational perimeters, and discovery of potential backdoors. The document should also include a risk matrix noting the operational risks associated with each technique and combinations thereof, along with mitigations to ensure safe and accurate execution. Please map each skill requirement back to the corresponding technique in a table format similar to what NIST recommends, and have a draft ready for review by the assessment team lead by end of next week.",
